      "prose": "The player character Mim arrives by train at Wordlark Hollow, a mountain resort village, and is welcomed by Station Manager Horace Pennyfeather. Mim's aunt Eloise was supposed to meet her but hasn't shown up, so Horace sends Mim to check the station while he investigates. Along the way we're introduced to the village's colorful residents: Bo Greyfoot, a practical air whale handler; Finnick Thorn, an enthusiastic cheese shop owner; and Penelope McCrick, a wealthy, snobbish widow — while Mim carries her suitcase and a handbook.",
